<title>UK: Main Novorossisk berth closed due to wind/swell.</title>
<headline>Main Novorossisk berth closed due to wind/swell.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The main berth at Russia's oil export port of Novorossiisk was closed on Tuesday due to high winds and swell, shipping sources said.</p>
<p>Berth one was closed at 0600 GMT due to high swell and southerly winds. The Lipetsk was currently loading gas oil at berth two but sources said it was unlikely that any further tankers would berth tonight as the high swells would make it dangerous for the line boats to work.</p>
<p>The next ship due to load was the Butron which will carry some 130,000 barrels of Urals crude oil. The tanker was originally due to start loading at 0800 GMT on April 12.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8978.</p>
